            functionalSolution = "public ConcurrentMap<String, Integer> aggregateParallel(List<OrderItem> items) {\n    return items.parallelStream()\n        .collect(Collectors.toConcurrentMap(\n            OrderItem::getProductId,\n            OrderItem::getQuantity,\n            Integer::sum,\n            ConcurrentHashMap::new\n        ));\n}",
            imperativeSolution = "public ConcurrentMap<String, Integer> aggregateParallel(List<OrderItem> items) throws InterruptedException {\n    ConcurrentMap<String, Integer> map = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();\n    ExecutorService pool = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(Runtime.getRuntime().availableProcessors());\n    for (OrderItem item : items) {\n        pool.submit(() -> map.merge(item.getProductId(), item.getQuantity(), Integer::sum));\n    }\n    pool.shutdown();\n    pool.awaitTermination(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS);\n    return map;\n}",
            comparisonInsight = "parallelStream automatically utilizes the ForkJoinPool and work-stealing algorithm, eliminating manual thread pool lifecycle management."
